# Build products.
*.o
*.d
*.a
*.elf
*.img
*.lst
*.map

# Per-board object tree for the archive (build/rpi3, build/rpi4, build/rpi5).
/build/

# Application blob trees, built by fpc-app.mk beside each consumer.
fpcblob/

# The record of which runtime a blob was compiled against, written beside the
# blob tree by fpc-app.mk.
*.rtl-stamp

# The card-route gate the M5, M6 and M7 examples carry: the Pascal side's
# undefined symbols, and the stamp that records the gate passing on them.
# Both are read out of the objects on every build.
no-card-route.stamp
pascal-undefined.txt

# The throwaway target name Circle's Rules.mk attaches its own link rule to.
.circle-unused.*

# The Free Pascal source this library builds against, reached as a symlink to
# the editing copy in the parent repository. The name is held for the submodule
# that takes its place, so the link is never committed here.
/fpc

# THE CIRCLE WORLDS ARE NOT SOURCE. Each is gigabytes of configured, built
# framework plus newlib and libc++, produced by circle-libsdl2's `make deps`
# and reproducible from its pins. Where they come from is docs/BUILDING.md.
/circle-stdlib-rpi3/
/circle-stdlib-rpi4/
/circle-stdlib-rpi5/
